NAME
    cat - print a file

SYNOPSIS
    cat <file>

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the contents of <file> to standard output. Streams the file in
    chunks, so a file of any size prints without being held whole in memory.
    Relative paths resolve against the current directory.

EXAMPLES
    cat notes.txt
    cat notes.txt | grep TODO

SEE ALSO
    more, ls, write
